>> title: Baklava
>> category: Bars & Brownies
>> tags: filo, pistachio, walnuts, middle eastern, oven, syrup
>> counters: Shawarma Counter, Bakery
>> aka: baklava, baklawa, bakhlava, baclava, baklawah, pistachio baklava, walnut baklava, filo nut pastry
>> pairs-with: attar, maamoul
>> servings: 24
>> time: 7 hr 30 min
>> slack: unforgiving — cold syrup onto a hot tray or hot syrup onto a cold one; matched temperatures and the filo goes soggy and stays that way
>> step.1: clarify the butter, skim it clear
>> step.2: chop the nuts coarse with the spice
>> step.3: layer the filo, butter every sheet
>> step.4: cut into diamonds before it bakes
>> step.5: bake at 325°F 1 1/4 hr
>> step.6: pour cold syrup over the hot tray, stand 4 hr

Melt @unsalted butter{1%cup}(225 g) over low heat without stirring, skim the foam off the top and pour the clear gold layer off the milky sediment, leaving that behind.

Chop @shelled pistachios{2%cups}(250 g) and @walnuts{1%cup}(115 g) coarse with @granulated sugar{2%Tbs}(25 g) and @ground cinnamon{1/2%tsp} — pulsed to a powder they pack into a paste, and the layer wants to stay rubble.

Layer @filo pastry{1%lb}(450 g; thawed overnight in the fridge) in a buttered #9x13 pan{}, brushing every single sheet with @&(~2)clarified butter{} and stopping halfway to spread @&(~1)nut mixture{} in an even bed.

Cut @&(~1)assembled tray{} all the way through to the base in parallel diagonals, into diamonds, **before** it goes anywhere near the oven.

Bake @&(~1)cut baklava{} in the #oven{} at 325°F (160°C) ~bake{1 1/4%hr}, until it is deep gold right through to the middle sheets.

Pour @attar{2%cups}(475 mL; straight from the fridge) evenly over @&(~1)hot baklava{} the moment it comes out — it will hiss and settle — then ~stand{4%hr} uncovered before cutting the diamonds free.
